{"name":"Mascarpone Ice Cream","permalink":"mascarpone-ice-cream","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/MascarponeIceCream.scala","source":"George","description":"A simple yet decadent ice cream recipe, no churn needed.","tagline":"Don't eat too much at once...","notes":["You can substitute marmalade for blackberries, cinnamon or any ingredient you fancy. Just be careful not to choose anything too watery, or you'll get ice crystals forming. It's also lovely plain.","I tend to double up this recipe to make enough for a few days.\n\nYou can use up the egg whites by making <a href=\"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/easy-chocolate-mousse\" rel=\"nofollow\">chocolate mousse</a>."],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Pudding"],"inherited_tags":[],"image":{"src":"https://i.reciba.se/ice-cream.jpg","width":1080,"height":1080},"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Mascarpone","quantity":"230g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Eggs","quantity":"2","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Icing Sugar","quantity":"60g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Vanilla Essence","quantity":"1 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Carefully separate the egg yolks using your hands or spoons. Put aside the egg whites for another recipe.","Whisk the egg yolks and sugar in a bowl, with an electric mixer, until thick and light in colour.","Add the mascarpone cheese and continue whisking until thoroughly mixed.","Decant into a freezer suitable dish and freeze for at least 6 hours."]}